    "result_text": "No lingering references. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), touching three files, each in its proper place:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced the derived `getMembershipTier()` getter with `getMembershipLevel()`. It starts at 1, adds 1 when an email is present, adds 1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, and caps at 3 (`Math.min(level, 3)`) \u2014 leaving level 4 reserved for tenure. The old `householdSize`-based `GOLD` logic is gone, per the new spec.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Swapped the `membershipTier` schema (string enum GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) for a `membershipLevel` integer field (`int32`, min 1, max 3, read-only). This regenerates `OwnerDto` at build time, and MapStruct auto-maps the new getter by property name \u2014 so `membershipTier` no longer appears in responses and `membershipLevel` takes its place.\n\n3. **`rest/audit/OwnerAuditLogger.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (via `owner.getMembershipLevel()`) instead of the tier, as the spec requires for anything that recorded the tier.\n\nVerification:\n- `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` asserts `$.membershipLevel == 3` for an owner with an email and no namesakes (1 + email + namesake0 = 3), which passes.\n- The audit output confirms the new format: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-18 membershipLevel=3`.\n- No remaining references to `membershipTier` / GOLD / SILVER / BRONZE anywhere in the source.",
